= Purpose

I intend for this document to serve as a post-event analysis report on what was done during this work \(from my perspective and those I may interview) for the benefit of myself, my fellow organizers, other organizers-to-be, and the community at large.

This document may serve as a potential list of do's and don't's for others looking to make similar organizational efforts in Starkville, or maybe even perhaps municipalities in general that are similar to our own \(e.g., small, college town, caring population).

Finally, I am writing this because I was asked to, and I like to be helpful.

I originally had a section on the timeline of this issue, but I realized that the exact timeline is not really important for a few reasons:

+ Every situation is different; the timelines will differ, sometimes drastically, between different companies, local governments, and local communities. Why our timeline worked may not apply.
+ The order of these steps isn't super relevant. The point is that we organized and organized \(somewhat) effectively, not that we held some certain number of meetings whithin a certain amount of time, or sent a certain amount of messages.
+ Organizing is more "fuzzy" than most problems I usually work on. With my engineering background, I'm used to following a certain list of steps when troubleshooting an issue or working on a solution to a problem. These efforts were most certainly not like that, but I believe the general insights we offer below may help offer guidance!

If you are interested in a timeline of big events, you can see the #link("https://starkvillecmf.org/#/archive/timeline")[timeline on website], but this timeline is from before the P&Z meeing on 2026-08-11 and has not been updated since then. \
For anyone still interested in a more detailed play-by-play, I may be able to provide a timeline of key organizational events later.

